resent a significant leap forward in how AI agents can interact with content management systems like Umbraco.</p><p>Traditionally, integrating AI with CMS platforms required custom APIs, complex authentication flows, and significant development effort. MCP servers standardize this interaction, providing a consistent interface that AI agents can use to read and modify content.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"fd01227d-504d-4ece-8e49-66455ca04496","key":"d0907186-1ccd-49ad-b918-8d06fa78b11b","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.MediaPicker3","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"image","value":[{"key":"b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4890-b1c2-d3e4f5a6b7c8","mediaKey":"fa081c45-3e6c-4617-82f8-8240fe1db1f7","mediaTypeAlias":"Image","crops":[],"focalPoint":null}]},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"caption","value":"Code on screen - the future of development"}]},{"contentTypeKey":"b7ec7bf1-ac85-452f-8ee2-e67ff8c02d31","key":"6b17dcde-1d2a-4902-8cd6-ba4697c6f019","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"text","value":{"markup":"<p>With MCP servers, AI agents can:</p><ul><li>Query content types, document types, and media</li><li>Create and update pages and media</li><li>Publish and unpublish content</li><li>Manage the entire content lifecycle</li></ul><p>This standardization reduces the barrier to entry for AI integration and makes it possible for non-developers to leverage AI capabilities.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"24556405-e126-4846-a34e-737d8be47123","key":"0a54284a-f4cd-484e-ba94-6b45bb3be376","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextArea","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"quote","value":"MCP is not just a protocol, it's a paradigm shift in how we think about AI and content management."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"attribution","value":"Umbraco Core Team"}]}],"settingsData":[],"expose":[{"contentKey":"e83987ec-e423-4909-b237-0c011ee02461","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"d0907186-1ccd-49ad-b918-8d06fa78b11b","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"6b17dcde-1d2a-4902-8cd6-ba4697c6f019","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"0a54284a-f4cd-484e-ba94-6b45bb3be376","culture":null,"segment":null}]}}],"urls":["/mcp-servers-the-future-of-ai-integration/"],"docType":"blogPost","template":"blogPost"}
{"id":"c67a5096-0062-4129-950a-843abca2b652","name":"Building a Blog with MCP and Umbraco","path":"WWW / Blog / Building a Blog with MCP and Umbraco","docTypeId":"d648c2bc-d50b-4398-8cfa-a5e1af1c5796","templateId":"7c08bd13-134a-4570-b516-0e9719cd56d9","state":"Published","domains":[],"values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"title","value":"Building a Blog with MCP and Umbraco"},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.DateTime","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"publishDate","value":"2026-10-05 10:00:00"},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextArea","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"excerpt","value":"Step-by-step guide to creating a complete blog site using MCP servers with Umbraco CMS."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.MediaPicker3","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"listingImage","value":[{"key":"c3d4e5f6-a7b8-4901-b2c3-d4e5f6a7b8c9","mediaKey":"0c25998b-4131-49ed-8a16-47811fc30fd5","mediaTypeAlias":"Image","crops":[],"focalPoint":null}]},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.BlockGrid","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"body","value":{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"a9438d9a-da23-4c4e-9da1-67b26ab1e9cc","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"d775fd4a-5106-4f71-8d9e-9d885bd30a43","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"9a45f37e-ca67-4c5b-bf19-f83e5e5272dc","settingsKey":null},{"$type":"BlockGridLayoutItem","columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1,"areas":[],"contentKey":"a9d55b62-2228-4393-ab55-90faed743e7d","settingsKey":null}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"b7ec7bf1-ac85-452f-8ee2-e67ff8c02d31","key":"a9438d9a-da23-4c4e-9da1-67b26ab1e9cc","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"text","value":{"markup":"<p>In this guide, we'll walk through the process of building a complete blog site using MCP servers with Umbraco CMS.</p><p>The combination of MCP's standardized protocol and Umbraco's flexible content management creates a powerful platform for AI-driven content creation and management.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"b7ec7bf1-ac85-452f-8ee2-e67ff8c02d31","key":"d775fd4a-5106-4f71-8d9e-9d885bd30a43","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.RichText","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"text","value":{"markup":"<p>Here's what we built:</p><ol><li>Created document types for blog front page and blog posts</li><li>Set up block types for rich text, images, and quotes</li><li>Imported images from Unsplash</li><li>Created content using MCP tools</li><li>Published everything</li></ol><p>The entire process was driven through MCP server calls, demonstrating how AI agents can manage content without direct database access or custom API development.</p>","blocks":{"layout":{},"contentData":[],"settingsData":[],"expose":[]}}}]},{"contentTypeKey":"24556405-e126-4846-a34e-737d8be47123","key":"9a45f37e-ca67-4c5b-bf19-f83e5e5272dc","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextArea","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"quote","value":"The future of content management is AI-assisted, and MCP is the bridge that makes it possible."},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"attribution","value":"Claude Code Developer"}]},{"contentTypeKey":"fd01227d-504d-4ece-8e49-66455ca04496","key":"a9d55b62-2228-4393-ab55-90faed743e7d","values":[{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.MediaPicker3","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"image","value":[{"key":"d4e5f6a7-b8c9-4012-b3d4-e5f6a7b8c9d0","mediaKey":"70d27121-9ad8-40f1-8522-3a5052e82a09","mediaTypeAlias":"Image","crops":[],"focalPoint":null}]},{"editorAlias":"Umbraco.TextBox","culture":null,"segment":null,"alias":"caption","value":"Network connections - the power of MCP"}]}],"settingsData":[],"expose":[{"contentKey":"a9438d9a-da23-4c4e-9da1-67b26ab1e9cc","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"d775fd4a-5106-4f71-8d9e-9d885bd30a43","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"9a45f37e-ca67-4c5b-bf19-f83e5e5272dc","culture":null,"segment":null},{"contentKey":"a9d55b62-2228-4393-ab55-90faed743e7d","culture":null,"segment":null}]}}],"urls":["/building-a-blog-with-mcp-and-umbraco/"],"docType":"blogPost","template":"blogPost"}
